Read fluid dynamics from zero (@fd-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/University-Physics-Volume-1.lingua#r_2W7QCEHZ45XDB3AWVG9NTV36F6", #source "../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18", #source "../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J", #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-and-Engineering-Chakraborty.lingua#r_31BBWRVBVVYRX6MZNTND5FZYF2", #fluid-dynamics "Observe-a-fluid-and-the-service-it-provides.lingua#r_2N3M0S840BRKVXMQ7QPNK77X5Z") { r_1JWVG3WSPPTZW4BP2N1BZPPZ12
**Read:** [University Physics Volume 1 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-1.lingua#r_2W7QCEHZ45XDB3AWVG9NTV36F6), chapter 14 in full, with the necessary mechanics chapters; [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18), the complete introductory text over this sequence; [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J), all eight chapters progressively; [Introduction to Fluid Mechanics and Fluid Engineering — Suman Chakraborty](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-and-Engineering-Chakraborty.lingua#r_31BBWRVBVVYRX6MZNTND5FZYF2), the complete public lecture progression.

Begin with a tap, a breeze, a drain or a liquid moving through a narrow tube. Describe what you can observe before giving the flow a technical name. A reader need not already know calculus to make these observations; the mathematical steps enter as the questions become quantitative.

Read the entire fluid-mechanics chapter in [University Physics Volume 1 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-1.lingua#r_2W7QCEHZ45XDB3AWVG9NTV36F6), revisiting its preceding mechanics chapters when force, momentum or energy is unfamiliar. Study all of [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18) as the introductory engineering development, with all eight chapters of [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J) as a Portuguese account of the same foundations and transport connections. Attempt substantial unfamiliar problems before using worked solutions. [Introduction to Fluid Mechanics and Fluid Engineering — Suman Chakraborty](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-and-Engineering-Chakraborty.lingua#r_31BBWRVBVVYRX6MZNTND5FZYF2) supplies a complete lecture companion.

Then work through all of [Intermediate Fluid Mechanics — James Liburdy](../sources/Intermediate-Fluid-Mechanics-Liburdy.lingua#r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N) and [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), including their mathematical development. [Fluid Mechanics — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Analytical-Fluid-Mechanics-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_075CGXNA8WHV26ZW53C7XTQ48V) supplies a sustained alternative analytical treatment and further exercises. [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ) provides demanding problems and examinations, and [Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P) extends the methods. Later readings deepen turbulence, interfaces, multiple phases, computation and physical evidence. Keep a worked account of one real fluid system as the meaning of each term becomes clearer.

**Continue:** [Observe a fluid and the service it provides](Observe-a-fluid-and-the-service-it-provides.lingua#r_2N3M0S840BRKVXMQ7QPNK77X5Z).

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics — motion, forces, transport and evidence](../Fluid-dynamics.lingua#r_7PQW1WDHK708BFV23MD8ET61VZ).
